W computation details:
```
theorem extra_gaussEntropyData {τ0 t1 : ℝ} (ht1 : t1 < τ0) {t : ℝ} (ht : t ≤ t1) :
    (gaussEntropyData τ0 t1 ht1 t).extra = Real.log (4 * Real.pi * (τ0 - t)) - 1
```
`extra D = ∫ x, (D.f x - D.n) * D.ρ x`. Unfold: `∫ (S/(4τ) + log(4πτ) - 2) * gaussDensity τ`. Split:
`∫ (S/(4τ))*ρ + ∫ (log(4πτ) - 2)*ρ` (needs integrability for `integral_add`, or use `integral_congr` + known values). Actually easier: show pointwise equality to a sum of two integrable functions, then use `integral_add`:
```
have h1 : Integrable (fun x => (1/(4*τ)) * (radSq x * gaussDensity τ x)) := (integrable_radSq_mul_exp_neg_mul_radSq ...).const_mul ... congr
have h2 : Integrable (fun x => (Real.log (4πτ) - 2) * gaussDensity τ x) := ...
rw [show (fun x => (f x - 2) * ρ x) = fun x => (1/(4τ)) * (radSq x * gaussDensity τ x) + (log(4πτ)-2) * gaussDensity τ x by funext x; unfold gaussPotential gaussDensity; field_simp; ring]
rw [integral_add h1 h2, integral_const_mul, integral_radSq_mul_gaussDensity τ hτ, integral_const_mul, integral_gaussDensity τ hτ]
field_simp; ring
```
The expected result: `(1/(4τ))*(4τ) + (log(4πτ)-2)*1 = 1 + log(4πτ) - 2 = log(4πτ) - 1`. ✓

Then:
```
theorem W_gaussEntropyData ... :
    (gaussEntropyData ... t).W = Real.log (4 * Real.pi * (τ0 - t)) := by
  rw [EntropyData.W_eq, F_gaussEntropyData ht1 ht, extra_gaussEntropyData ht1 ht]
  -- τ * (1/τ) + (log - 1) = log
  field_simp
  ring
